## Special Thanks

### Dependency Projects
We thank the following open-source projects for providing important foundational support to Pilot:

- [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go) - High-performance RPC framework
- [etcd](https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd) - Distributed key-value storage system
- [Protocol Buffers](https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf) - Data serialization protocol
- [Go](https://golang.org/) - Programming language and standard library

### Design Inspiration
- [grpc-gateway](https://github.com/grpc-ecosystem/grpc-gateway) - gRPC to HTTP proxy
- [Istio](https://istio.io/) - Service mesh platform
- [Envoy](https://envoyproxy.io/) - Cloud-native proxy

### Community Support
We thank the following communities and organizations for their support:

- [Go Community](https://golang.org/community/)
- [CNCF](https://www.cncf.io/) - Cloud Native Computing Foundation
- [GitHub Community](https://github.com/)

## How to Become a Contributor

We welcome all forms of contributions! Please check the [Contributing Guide](CONTRIBUTING.md) to learn how to participate in the project.

### Contribution Types
- 🐛 Bug fixes
- ✨ New feature development
- 📝 Documentation improvements
- 🧪 Test case writing
- 🌐 Internationalization support
- 🎨 UI/UX design
- 📊 Performance optimization
- 🛡️ Security improvements

### Contributor Benefits
- Listed in AUTHORS file
- Acknowledged in project releases
- Participate in project decision discussions
- Priority technical support

## Ranking Explanation

This file is ordered as follows:
1. Project founder and core maintainers
2. Code contributors (sorted by commit time)
3. Documentation contributors
4. Community contributors
5. Specially thanked organizations and individuals

## Update Frequency

The AUTHORS file is updated with each major version release. If you find any omissions or errors, please submit an Issue or Pull Request.

---

**Note:** If you do not wish to be listed in the AUTHORS file, please send an email to privacy@pilot.dev and we will process it promptly.

